WEBVTT

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:04.030
Many years ago, when I started my own journey into the Quran,

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:07.510
I found myself having a lot of questions as I read the translation.

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:10.620
How come there's so much repetition in the Quran? This was already talked about

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:13.740
why is it being talked about again? How come there's no chronological order?

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:16.000
How come some chapters are long and some are short?

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:18.370
How come they're not in some sort of subject order?

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:18.840
Uh,

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:22.300
And how come, you know, there's a story and it's only a little bit over here

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.550
and then some little bit over there and some little bit over there again,

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:27.900
and questions like these kept popping up in my mind as I read the text.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:29.960
It wasn't like any other book that I had ever read.

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:32.980
And so as I started exploring the answers to these questions,

00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:35.680
I realized that not only were the answers to

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:38.540
these questions some things that make the Quran unique,

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:41.790
but it actually is something that makes the Quran truly divine.

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:43.680
It's incredible.

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:47.640
And it's humbling that what started off as criticism became the very reason that I

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:51.160
was strengthened in my faith that this book can only be from Allah.

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:55.330
This is what inspired me to create my first ever Quran course called Divine Speech.

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:58.400
I traveled around the world teaching it and actually what I feel

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:02.880
this is the second step that I would like you to take in your journey to the Quran,

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:07.000
going through that course that I created to answer these and more questions.

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:09.920
The purpose of it by the end of this course is two things.

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:13.050
One, you learn things about the Quran that you might not have known before,

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:13.590
of course.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:18.220
And two that, you're going to come out saying, Wow, this can't be from a human being.

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:19.420
This has to be divine.

00:01:19.430 --> 00:01:22.320
It will reinforce your faith and confidence in

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:24.230
the divine beauty and power of the Quran.

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:26.360
So let's begin this journey: Divine Speech.